      "id": "GENUS_EURYPYGA",
      "name": "Eurypyga",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "A monotypic genus of elegantly patterned wading bird with an extraordinary hidden display. The Sunbittern's subtle brown, grey and black plumage conceals brilliant orange, red and black bands on the wings that are flashed open in a dramatic sunburst display during courtship and threat. It inhabits forest streams and rivers of the Neotropics.",
